<ToolPage figure="loupe" title="Incident Room" lede="Something is wrong in production. Read the evidence, find the root cause, choose the fix.">
  <IncidentRoom client:load />
  <Fragment slot="notes">
    <h2>How to play</h2>
    <p>Read the report, then open only the evidence you think will help. Every piece you open costs points. When you are ready, pick the root cause. A wrong guess costs points and tells you why it is wrong. After a correct diagnosis, choose the best fix.</p>
    <h2>What it teaches</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Most failures are not the model. The data, the pipeline, the cache, the limits and the tools are usually to blame first.</li>
      <li>One decisive clue is worth more than ten logs. Learn where to look: the finish reason, the prompt breakdown, the retrieved passages, the operator report.</li>
      <li>A good fix addresses the cause, makes the next failure visible and stops it spreading.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The ten incidents are composites of failure patterns that recur in real systems. Names and numbers are invented.</p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolPage>
